{# ═══ PROPHET CARD v1 — the flagship standout-stock card, shared by the US / China / HK /
   Canada / International prophet boards (operator-ratified redesign, 2026-07-21 session).

   The contract (fixed slots — the layout NEVER moves between cards or states):
     · chart-first hero: the row's pre-rendered sparkline SVG, recolored to the verb hue,
       with the verb chip + ⚠N flags (top-left) and the live price pill (top-right) overlaid
     · ONE verb from a 5-word vocabulary: buy / near / wait / hold / avoid — only BUY solid
     · ONE score slot ("Edge") — absent value renders an em-dash, never reflows (Canada
       Branch-B keeps its score suppression by passing edge=None)
     · identity: ticker + name on one line, sector alone underneath
     · 4-stage lifecycle tracker: Bottoming → Turning → Ready → Trend (stage 0 = all muted)
     · contextual zone footer: ZONE range / muted pending range / "sets on confirmation" /
       RE-ADD range / "no zone" — plus an optional labelled Added / 入榜 board-membership
       chip (`.pv-added`, param `added_date`, engine/prophet_board_since.py) and the
       separate legacy per-row `date` chip (`.pv-dt`) for callers whose date really is
       per-row and honest (the plan-book cards). Candidate-board callers pass `date: none`
       and pass `added_date` instead — the two slots are independent and never merged.
     · one hue per card: glow edge, chart, chip, score, tracker and zone label all follow the
       verb via --pvh. Hues are the dedicated --pv-* tokens (theme.css): green-up/red-down
       in English and red-up/green-down under html[data-lang="zh"].

   ONE DELIBERATE EXCEPTION TO THE ONE-HUE LAW — .pv-live (Prophet Live P1, spec §5.1).
   The card's hue encodes THE NIGHTLY VERDICT. The ◐ live chip belongs to TODAY'S TAPE: a
   provisional, un-graded intraday read that only tonight's close settles. Painting it --pvh
   would render a "below range" caution GREEN on a Buy card — i.e. it would claim the live
   state is part of the confirmed verdict, which is the exact false claim the prophet_live
   program exists to avoid. So the live chip carries its own --plvc (provisional blue) or
   --pv-wait (caution), and the two chips stay distinguishable by glyph as well: ⚡ = nightly
   (keeps --pvh, untouched), ◐ = live. Do not "repair" this into the one-hue law.
     · prior disclosures survive, demoted: cautions / sector stance / chase / extension /
       earnings-window → the ⚠N popover (pure CSS hover/focus-within, no JS dependency);
       score meaning → Edge data-tip. The verdict sentence + entry headline USED to ride a
       verb-chip data-tip; the operator removed it 2026-08-03 (see the chip in the markup)
       because it only re-worded the chip, tracker and zone footer the reader can already
       see. The five builders no longer compute or pass a top-level `tip_en`/`tip_zh`, and
       the chip takes no tip. Do not reintroduce one. (The similarly-named keys that DO
       still render are unrelated: `trigger.tip_en`/`tip_zh` on the ⚡ chip, `edge_tip_en`/
       `edge_tip_zh` on the score, and `marks[].tip_en`/`tip_zh` on the sub-line chips.)

   The macro is deliberately dumb: every market-specific derivation (verb mapping, stage
   mapping, flag folding, zone kind) happens in the calling board template where the row
   fields live. Callers pass a single `cx` dict:
     href tk sym mkt price_txt show_change name name_zh sec sec_zh flag verb edge
     edge_tip_en edge_tip_zh stage spark zone_kind zone_lo zone_hi date flags triage
     trigger — OPTIONAL {kind: 'fired'|'imminent', tip_en, tip_zh}: the fresh
       entry-trigger chip (presentation merge of the Top-setups board, 2026-07-24
       masterplan). Absent key → no chip, layout unchanged; the verb stays the
       card's ruling stance (a Wait card with ⚡ = fired trigger, extended price).
       'imminent' renders dashed (pending semantics). Like every element, the chip
       follows the card hue --pvh (one-hue law).
     featured — OPTIONAL bool (prophet board priority engine, 2026-08-02): the
       glow cohort. Adds .pv-featured — a soft bullish aura + a full-bleed lit rail.
       It is the ONE element that does NOT follow --pvh: the aura is pinned to
       --pv-buy because "featured" MEANS the pick cohort, and it must follow the
       active language's bullish convention even if a future stage rule ever lets
       a non-buy verb be featured. Callers
       must not also pass triage on a featured row (one accent per card) — the
       aura supersedes the triage ring.
     stage_key — OPTIONAL slug ('live'|'setting_up'|'ran'|'basing'|'blocked'): emitted
       as data-stage so a board can filter its grid client-side with pure CSS.
       ('basing' was added by the D18 bottom-watch shelf, engine/us_board_rank.py.)
     marks — OPTIONAL list of {k, en, zh, tip_en?, tip_zh?}: the sub-line chip row
       between the sector and the lifecycle tracker. `k` picks the visual weight:
       'feat' (filled green, the strongest), 'new' (accent outline), 'warm'
       (amber — a context event just turned), 'lane' / 'theme' (plain muted),
       'nck' (hollow dashed — the one chip that reports an ABSENCE, see its rule).
       ABSENT key → no row at all, card height unchanged (every non-US board).
       EMPTY list → an empty row that still RESERVES its height, so a board using
       marks keeps the tracker and zone rows aligned across a grid row even when one
       card has nothing to mark. Pass `none`, not `[]`, to opt out per-board.
   Live-quote contract preserved: the price keeps class "nb-px" + data-sym/data-mkt
   (templates/live.js binds .nb-px[data-sym]). When a caller passes show_change=true,
   the same pill gains an adjacent "nb-chg" sibling bound to the same canonical symbol;
   it MUST stay outside .nb-px because live.js replaces the price node's textContent. #}
{% macro t(en, zh='') -%}<span class="l-en">{{ en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ zh if zh else en }}</span>{%- endmacro %}

{# ═══ P-MP1-SHELL §4b/§10 — THE 7-CELL LIFECYCLE LADDER ═══════════════════════════
   Renders MP-1-prophet-board.md §4b's cell set VERBATIM (labels/order/weight
   grammar), against `.mx-ladder--board`/`.mx-cell`/`.mx-cap`/`.mx-mark` — the
   DS-PR-0 primitives (theme.css, gate G-B) — never new CSS here beyond the
   template-scoped .pv-mark/.pv-life additions above/below.

   COUNT LAW (ruling §6, MP-1 §7 "canonical counts"): every number this macro
   prints is a published field off `book` — `lifecycle_counts`,
   `lifecycle_live_total`, `lifecycle_grand_total` — NEVER a row count computed
   here. `book` is ALWAYS the FULL (unsliced) book, regardless of tier gating:
   docs/TIER_PREVIEW_PATTERN.md — "state and totals are free, names are paid" —
   so life_gate never reaches this macro and never should.

   FILTER STATE is entirely CLIENT-SIDE (this is a statically generated page,
   baked once per build with no per-request query string to read): every cell
   bakes `aria-pressed="false"`; dashboard.html.j2's inline script reads
   `location.search`/legacy `location.hash` on load and toggles the pressed
   state + `data-lifef` (MP-1 §7 URL law) — mirrors the existing `data-stagef`
   CSS-filter idiom (theme.css / dashboard.html.j2 ~880-891) exactly, keyed on
   `data-life` instead of `data-stage`.

   STATES (§10, Amendment 2 ratified): `book` None → LOADING (skeletons shimmer
   the COUNTS only, never dashes/zeros — the em dash already means
   "published and absent", ruling §6 fn.1, so a loading dash would make one
   glyph carry two facts). `book` present, `early_turn_watch` key absent from
   `book.intake` → the Watch cell renders the KEY-ABSENCE em-dash + the
   `.ladder-absence` disclosure line. `early_turn_watch` present (even empty,
   Amendment 1 P-K19) → Watch renders its normal zero-count cell like every
   other live cell, no disclosure line. #}
{% macro mx_ladder(book, error=false) %}
{%- set _CELLS_LIVE = ['watch','ready','entered','delivering','overtime','invalidated'] -%}
{%- set _LEX_EN = {'watch':'Watch','ready':'Ready','entered':'Entered','delivering':'Delivering','overtime':'Overtime','invalidated':'Invalidated','resolved':'Resolved'} -%}
{%- set _LEX_ZH = {'watch':'观察','ready':'就绪','entered':'入场','delivering':'达标','overtime':'超时','invalidated':'失效','resolved':'已结'} -%}
{%- set _NUMWORD = {1:'one',2:'two',3:'three',4:'four',5:'five',6:'six',7:'seven'} -%}
{%- if error %}
{#- §10 error state, Amendment 2's C8-B shipped three-section string (supersedes
   Amendment 1's two-section draft — the trading-record strip is a third
   surviving section the promise must cover). `.mx-error` is the DS-PR-0
   primitive (theme.css). Retry reloads the page — this is a static-build
   artifact-read failure, not a client-side fetch, so the only "retry" that
   means anything is asking the browser for the page again (the NEXT render
   is what actually fixes it; this button just gives the reader something to
   press rather than a dead end). -#}
<div class="mx-error" role="alert">
  <b>!</b>
  <span>
    <span class="l-en">The board didn’t load. Candidates, Groups and the record below are current.</span>
    <span class="l-zh">看板未能加载。下方的候选、板块与战绩仍是最新。</span>
    <button type="button" class="ladder-clear" style="min-height:40px;min-width:40px;margin-top:6px" onclick="location.reload()">{{ t('Retry', '重试') }}</button>
  </span>
</div>
{%- elif not book %}
<div class="ladder-headline"><span class="skel sk-head" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ladder-nl">{{ t('live setups today','个跟踪中计划') }}</span></div>
<div class="mx-ladder mx-ladder--board" role="group" aria-busy="true" aria-label="Lifecycle counts loading">
  {% for k in _CELLS_LIVE %}
  <div class="mx-cell{% if loop.last %} mx-cell--last-live{% endif %}"><span class="mx-cap mx-cap--{{ k }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="skel sk-n" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="mx-cell-l">{{ t(_LEX_EN[k], _LEX_ZH[k]) }}</span></div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="mx-ladder-gap" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="mx-cell mx-cell--term"><span class="mx-cap mx-cap--resolved" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="skel sk-n" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="mx-cell-l">{{ t(_LEX_EN.resolved, _LEX_ZH.resolved) }}</span></div>
  <div class="ladder-termnote">{{ t('not in today’s count', '不计入上方总数') }}</div>
</div>
{%- else -%}
{%- set _counts = book.get('lifecycle_counts') or {} -%}
{%- set _live_total = book.get('lifecycle_live_total') or 0 -%}
{%- set _watch_present = 'early_turn_watch' in (book.get('intake') or {}) -%}
{%- set _published = _CELLS_LIVE|length - (0 if _watch_present else 1) -%}
<div class="ladder-headline"><span class="ladder-n fig">{{ _live_total }}</span><span class="ladder-nl">{{ t('live setups today','个跟踪中计划') }}</span><span class="ladder-sub">{{ t('the ' ~ _NUMWORD.get(_published, _published) ~ ' published cells below add up to this number', '下方 ' ~ _published ~ ' 个已发布状态合计') }}</span></div>
<div class="mx-ladder mx-ladder--board" role="group" aria-label="Filter setups by lifecycle" id="us-life-ladder">
  {% for k in _CELLS_LIVE %}
  {%- set _absent = (k == 'watch') and not _watch_present -%}
  {%- set _n = _counts.get(k) or 0 -%}
  <button type="button" class="mx-cell{% if loop.last %} mx-cell--last-live{% endif %}" data-life="{{ k }}" aria-pressed="false"{% if _absent %} data-absent="1"{% elif _n == 0 %} data-zero="1"{% endif %}>
    <span class="mx-cap mx-cap--{{ k }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="mx-cell-n fig">{{ '—' if _absent else _n }}</span>
    <span class="mx-cell-l">{{ t(_LEX_EN[k], _LEX_ZH[k]) }}</span>
  </button>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="mx-ladder-gap" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <button type="button" class="mx-cell mx-cell--term" data-life="resolved" aria-pressed="false">
    <span class="mx-cap mx-cap--resolved" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="mx-cell-n fig">{{ _counts.get('resolved') or 0 }}</span>
    <span class="mx-cell-l">{{ t(_LEX_EN.resolved, _LEX_ZH.resolved) }}</span>
  </button>
  <div class="ladder-termnote">{{ t('not in today’s count', '不计入上方总数') }}</div>
</div>
{%- if not _watch_present %}
{#- Repair round, finding S5: the ZH string must be MP-1 §10's ratified
   string VERBATIM — the previous copy ("「观察」将在下一次收盘更新后发布。")
   was a paraphrase, not the ruled text. -#}
<p class="ladder-absence"><span class="mx-mark mx-mark--watch" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ t('Watch tier publishes from the next nightly.', '观察档自下一次夜间构建起发布。') }}</p>
{%- endif %}
<div class="ladder-foot">
  <span>{{ t('Sorted by priority — how ready a setup is today, not how likely it is to win.', '按优先级排序 — 数值越高表示越接近可操作，并不代表胜率更高。') }}
  <span class="help">?<span class="tip tip-wide"><span class="l-en">Each cell counts plan rows — one row per tracked commitment, so a name traded twice appears twice. Watch counts names with a live signal and no open plan yet. The six live cells add up to the headline; Resolved sits outside it, because a closed plan is record rather than inventory.</span><span class="l-zh">每一格统计的是「计划」条目——每条对应一次独立的跟踪，因此同一只股票若有两次操作，就会出现两次。「观察」统计的是已有信号、但尚未建立计划的股票。6 个状态相加等于标题数字；「已结」不计入其中，因为已平仓的计划属于历史战绩，不是当前持仓。</span></span></span></span>
  <button type="button" class="ladder-clear" id="us-life-clear" data-life="" hidden>{{ t('Clear filter','清除筛选') }}</button>
</div>
{%- endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro pv_css() %}
<style>
.pvcard{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--panel2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;color:var(--text);min-width:0;transition:transform .12s,box-shadow .12s,border-color .12s}
.pvcard:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);box-shadow:0 5px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.22);border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 55%,var(--line))}
.pv-buy{--pvh:var(--pv-buy);--pvh-ink:var(--ink-pv-buy,var(--pvh))}.pv-near{--pvh:var(--pv-near);--pvh-ink:var(--ink-pv-near,var(--pvh))}.pv-wait{--pvh:var(--pv-wait);--pvh-ink:var(--ink-pv-wait,var(--pvh))}.pv-hold{--pvh:var(--pv-hold);--pvh-ink:var(--pv-hold)}.pv-avoid{--pvh:var(--pv-avoid);--pvh-ink:var(--ink-pv-avoid,var(--pvh))}
{# P-MP1-SHELL §8a / Q7b — the "no read yet" (BLOCKED_DATA) card carries NO stance
   hue (DESIGN_NOTES.md: "an unavailable read is not a cautious read"). --pvh/--pvh-ink
   both resolve to --muted so every hue-driven element on the card (chart, chip, edge
   number, zone label, stage dots) renders in the same neutral ink the layout already
   uses for "nothing to report", rather than inventing a sixth hue. The verb chip's
   dashed border is the additional, load-bearing "this is absence, not a verdict" cue. #}
.pv-noread{--pvh:var(--muted);--pvh-ink:var(--muted)}
{# Selected via an ATTRIBUTE selector on the chip span's own `data-noread` marker
   (see the macro below), not a class or a plain descendant selector: two existing
   raw-source guards constrain the form here — tests/test_prophet_card_shared.py's
   verb-chip guard requires the chip's `class` attribute to stay literally exactly
   `class="pv-chip"` in the unrendered template source (so it can assert no
   `data-tip` attribute sits beside it), and
   tests/test_prophet_verb_ink_contrast.py's _rule() helper regex-matches the FIRST
   occurrence of the base chip selector text immediately followed by optional
   whitespace and an opening brace, anywhere in the raw file. An attribute selector
   satisfies both: `class="pv-chip"` in the macro markup never changes, and the
   selector text below never has "pv-chip" immediately followed by only
   whitespace-then-brace (the "[" breaks that match). #}
.pv-chip[data-noread]{border-style:dashed;background:transparent}
.pvcard::before{content:"";position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;height:3px;z-index:3;pointer-events:none;border-radius:12px 12px 0 0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--pvh),color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 12%,transparent) 90%);box-shadow:0 1px 8px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 45%,transparent)}
.pvcard.pv-triage::before{box-shadow:0 1px 12px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 70%,transparent)}
{# ── FEATURED GLOW (prophet board priority engine, G0.2 — 2026-08-02) ──────────
   The board's flagship "these are the picks" affordance, and the one place this
   design spends its boldness. ONE idea — the card is LIT — carried at three
   distances so it survives every way the board is looked at: the tinted body
   reads across a full-page scan, the aura separates the card from its neighbours
   at arm's length, and up close the card's own hue rail stops fading out and
   stays lit edge to edge.

   The tinted body is load-bearing, not decoration. A rim glow ALONE was tried
   first and it vanished in a dense 5-column grid where every card is already
   tinted by its own verb hue: on a 40-card screenshot only the chip separated
   featured from plain. Do not "clean this up" back to a bare ring.

   Deliberately STATIC: a dozen simultaneously pulsing cards on a dense dashboard
   is noise, and a still glow is legible at every distance — so there is no
   animation here and therefore no prefers-reduced-motion kill block to keep in
   sync (the strongest form of that compliance is having nothing to disable).

   The glow is pinned to --pv-buy, NOT --pvh (see the macro header). theme.css
   rebinds --pv-buy to the active language's bullish convention, so the featured
   treatment remains semantically bullish in both English and Chinese. Colour is
   never the only carrier either: every featured card also renders a
   "★ Featured / 精选" chip in its marks row (contrast-checked below). #}
{# TONE CALIBRATION (operator correction 2026-08-03, live-board review): the first
   shipped values washed the ENTIRE container green — background tints of 7%/8%
   with 50-60%-alpha auras read as "radioactive paint", worst on light where 8%
   green over #fff painted every featured card mint. The correction: the card BODY
   stays the normal panel/white — featured is a thin ring + a faint outer aura +
   the ★ chip, nothing more. Dark keeps a barely-there 2.5% lift (pure black
   panels swallow a ring alone); light gets NO tint at all. #}
.pvcard.pv-featured{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 2.5%,var(--panel2));
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 38%,var(--line));
  box-shadow:0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 24%,transparent),
             0 0 16px -6px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 32%,transparent),
             0 10px 26px -14px rgba(0,0,0,.7)}
{# hover must ADD the lift, not replace the aura (.pvcard:hover sets a bare shadow) #}
.pvcard.pv-featured:hover{border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 48%,var(--line));
  box-shadow:0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 30%,transparent),
             0 0 20px -6px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 40%,transparent),
             0 8px 22px -8px rgba(0,0,0,.5)}
.pvcard.pv-featured::before{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--pvh),color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 55%,transparent));
  box-shadow:0 1px 10px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 40%,transparent)}
{# Light theme: NO background tint — the operator's reference is a clean white
   card; featured reads through the ring, the whisper aura and the ★ chip. #}
html[data-theme="light"] .pvcard.pv-featured{background:#fff;
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 30%,var(--line));
  box-shadow:0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 16%,transparent),
             0 0 12px -6px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 22%,transparent),
             0 8px 20px -14px rgba(24,58,40,.22)}
html[data-theme="light"] .pvcard.pv-featured:hover{border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 40%,var(--line));
  box-shadow:0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 22%,transparent),
             0 0 16px -6px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 30%,transparent),
             0 8px 20px -10px rgba(24,58,40,.18)}
{# The ⚠ popover lives inside .pv-chart, so .pvcard{overflow:hidden} used to CLIP it:
   a 5-caution name rendered a 207px popover inside a 180px card and two whole rows —
   the sector stance and the "already moving" warning — were unreachable at any width.
   The card must therefore stop clipping while the popover is open. The chart, its
   sparkline and the zone row now round their OWN corners instead of borrowing the
   card's clip, so releasing it costs no square-corner artifact. NOTE: never give
   .pv-chart overflow:hidden to do this — that is the popover's own ancestor and would
   re-create the bug one level down.

   z-index is the SECOND half of the same fix and is not optional (2026-08-03): releasing
   the clip let the popover escape the card, but it still painted UNDER the next card in
   the grid. .pvcard:hover sets transform:translateY(-2px), and a non-none transform
   creates a stacking context — so .pv-cau-pop{z-index:30} is resolved INSIDE the hovered
   card, not against its siblings. Every later sibling .pvcard (position:relative,
   z-index:auto) therefore paints on top, and the popover was covered by the card to its
   right on every board (reported on us_stocks + hk_stocks; the partial is shared, so it
   was global). Lifting the CARD — the element that owns the stacking context — is what
   raises the popover with it; raising .pv-cau-pop further cannot work, because it is
   already at the top of a context that is itself too low. 40 clears sibling cards and the
   page's sticky chrome (max z-index 4 here) and stays far below the modal/LENS layers
   (1200+), so an open popover never outranks a dialog. #}
.pvcard:has(.pv-cau:hover),.pvcard:has(.pv-cau:focus-within){overflow:visible;z-index:40}
.pv-chart{position:relative;min-width:0;border-radius:11px 11px 0 0;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 3%,transparent)}
.pv-chart svg{display:block;width:100%;height:74px;border-radius:11px 11px 0 0}
{# spark recolor law (band contract): everything strokes the verb hue; filled shapes flip
   to hue fill. The builder-drawn buy-zone band (_spark_svg zone_lo/zone_hi/zone_state)
   relies on this exact split — its dashed edge lines carry NO fill attribute (only the
   stroke rule recolors them, dasharray survives) and its rect keeps a low fill-opacity
   ATTRIBUTE the fill override does not touch. Don't override fill-opacity/stroke-dasharray
   here without re-checking the band in the five *_library _spark_svg generators. #}
.pv-chart svg *{stroke:var(--pvh)!important}
.pv-chart svg [fill]:not([fill="none"]){fill:var(--pvh)!important;stroke:none!important}
.pv-nochart{height:74px}
.pv-ov{position:absolute;top:8px;display:flex;gap:5px;align-items:center;z-index:2;max-width:70%}
{# PRE-EXISTING BUG, fixed 2026-07-30 (P1 spec §5.3): this rule lived ONLY inside the
   @media (max-width:680px) block, so at DESKTOP width a left overlay that outgrew
   .pv-ov{max-width:70%} did not wrap — the excess chip clipped BEHIND the .pv-px price
   pill. Reachable today with verb + ⚡ + ⚠N on a 246px grid cell; the ◐ live chip would
   have made it routine. The overlay is absolutely positioned, so wrapping costs no card
   height and the grid is untouched — the second chip row sits over the sparkline. #}
.pv-ov.pv-ovl{flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:3px}
.pv-ovl{left:9px}.pv-ovr{right:9px}
.pv-chip{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1.35;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh,var(--muted)) 13%,var(--panel,#fff));color:var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh,var(--muted)));border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh,var(--muted))) 40%,transparent)}
/* solid Buy chip: ink-grade fill + panel ink — white on the raw hue was 3.61:1
   light / 2.51:1 dark at 10px/800 (the worst white-on-hue chip in the estate
   audit); panel-on-ink clears 4.5 in both themes and keeps the solid identity. */
.pv-buy .pv-chip{background:var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh,var(--up)));color:var(--panel,#fff);border-color:transparent}
.pvcard .pv-quote{display:inline-flex;align-items:baseline;gap:6px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--panel) 86%,transparent);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;padding:1px 6px;white-space:nowrap}
.pvcard .nb-px.pv-px,.pvcard .nb-chg.pv-chg{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;line-height:1.35;white-space:nowrap;margin:0}
.pvcard .nb-px.pv-px{color:var(--text)}
.pvcard .pv-ovr>.nb-px.pv-px{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--panel) 86%,transparent);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;padding:1px 6px}
.pvcard .pv-quote .pv-chg{color:var(--muted)}
{# live.js injects generic literal direction colors after this stylesheet. These
   more-specific rules deliberately win and route Prophet cards through the global
   semantic inks, whose --up/--down bases flip for the Chinese market convention. #}
.pvcard .pv-quote .pv-chg.up{color:var(--ink-up,var(--up))}
.pvcard .pv-quote .pv-chg.down{color:var(--ink-down,var(--down))}
.pvcard .pv-quote .pv-chg.stale{color:var(--muted);font-weight:700}
.pv-bd{padding:8px 11px 9px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;flex:1}
.pv-hd{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;min-width:0}
.pv-idw{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:6px;min-width:0;overflow:hidden}
.pv-tk{font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.01em;white-space:nowrap}
.pv-flg{font-size:12px;flex:none}
.pv-nm{font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;min-width:0}
.pv-edge{display:inline-flex;align-items:baseline;gap:4px;flex:none}
.pv-edl{font-size:9.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}
.pv-edn{font-size:14px;font-weight:800;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh));line-height:1}
.pv-edn.pv-edna{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;font-size:12px}
.pv-ind{font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);opacity:.85;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;margin-top:1px}
{# ── MARKS ROW (prophet board priority engine, 2026-08-02) ────────────────────
   One wrapping row of ≤1–2-word chips under the sector line. Four categorically
   DIFFERENT facts, in descending weight, so the row reads as a taxonomy rather
   than chip spam: rank (★ Featured) · recency (New) · a context event that just
   turned (amber) · setup shape and theme (both plain muted context, the demoted
   bottoming/continuation lane among them). The median card shows one muted chip.
   Contrast: every coloured chip's text is color-mix(<hue> 60%, var(--text)) over
   a 13–16% tint of the same hue on --panel2. That single formula clears WCAG AA
   in BOTH themes because --text itself inverts — measured ratios:
   featured 6.05 dark / 4.81 light · new 6.13 / 6.07 · warm 6.46 / 4.94.
   Do not "simplify" it to the raw token: raw --pv-buy on its own tint is 2.69:1
   in light mode, a fail. #}
{# min-height RESERVES the slot. The macro's founding contract is that the layout never
   moves between cards or states, and the tracker + zone rows are the landmarks the eye
   uses to compare cards across a grid row — a card with nothing to mark used to pull
   them ~18px up out of line with its neighbours. A caller that passes an EMPTY list
   (rather than omitting the key) opts into the reserved slot; a caller that omits
   `marks` entirely — every non-US board today — renders no row and no reservation. #}
.pv-mk{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:3px 4px;margin-top:4px;min-width:0;min-height:18px}
.pv-mk-i{font-size:9.5px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.45;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:6px;
  white-space:nowrap;max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;
  color:var(--muted);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 10%,transparent);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 22%,transparent)}
.pv-mk-feat{font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 60%,var(--text));
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 16%,var(--panel2));
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-buy) 44%,transparent)}
.pv-mk-new{font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 60%,var(--text));
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 13%,var(--panel2));
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--info) 38%,transparent)}
.pv-mk-warm{color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn) 60%,var(--text));
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn) 15%,var(--panel2));
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn) 38%,transparent)}
.pv-mk-theme{color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 55%,var(--text));
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 34%,transparent)}
{# Blow-off risk — the one marks chip that is a RISK read, so it borrows the caution
   button's ink family (.pv-cau-btn) rather than the soft --warn wash .pv-mk-warm uses
   for "Theme just turned".  Deliberately NOT a directional token: the zh board flips
   up/down inks (红涨绿跌) and a risk chip must read identically in both languages. #}
{# The 8% wash is measured, not taste: at the 17% this started on, the light theme
   computed 3.95:1 ink-on-fill — under AA, and under the sibling .pv-mk-feat's 4.84:1
   (9.5px/800 is NOT "large text", so 3:1 does not apply). Lightening the fill and
   keeping --ink-warn at full strength reads 6.89:1 dark / 4.77:1 light. #}
.pv-mk-blow{font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--ink-warn,var(--warn));
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn) 8%,var(--panel));
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink-warn,var(--warn)) 50%,transparent)}
{# 'adj' (W-L1, spec §4.3) — the overnight pass moved something on this name after the
   evening board. DESATURATED ON PURPOSE, and that is the whole point of the rule: at the
   marks row's normal formula — color-mix(<hue> 58%, --text) on a 12% tint — it came out
   the same blue as .pv-mk-new, which sits inches away on the same board and means
   something completely different ("new to the board" is a signal; "adjusted" is a
   receipt). Two meanings in one hue is a defect no amount of wording fixes. The fix is
   WEIGHT, not hue: 'adjusted' resolves toward --muted so it reads as the quietest thing
   in the row while 'new' keeps the saturated --info. That also matches what the mark is
   worth to the reader — the honest answer to "so what do I do" here is nothing; the card
   already shows the updated numbers. Measured on the real board, composited:
   5.01:1 dark / 5.28:1 light (mockups/refs/breathing-platform/verify_wl1.py).
   No markup change is needed: the macro renders pv-mk-{{ k }} for whatever `k` the
   caller passes, and 'adj' is deliberately NOT in _MK_NOTIP, so its tip renders —
   correct, because unlike feat/new this mark names something the reader cannot infer. #}
.pv-mk-adj{font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--prov-ink) 42%,var(--muted));
  background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--prov) 7%,transparent);
  border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--prov) 30%,transparent)}
{# 'nck' — THE ABSENCE CHIP (ANTICIPATION v1 per-row carrier, 2026-08-09).  Every
   other mark in this row states something that IS true of the name: it is featured,
   it is new, its theme turned, its 12-day move hit an extreme.  This one marks a
   slot where a reading should have been and wasn't — so it is drawn as the OUTLINE
   of a chip: no fill at all, a dashed hairline, muted ink.  The form is the message,
   and it needs no new hue; the featured aura is where this card spends its colour
   (Chanel's rule — take one accessory off).

   Dashed is BORROWED, not invented: .pv-trg-soon already uses a dashed border on
   this card for "pending, not settled".  Same grammar, one level quieter.

   Sentence case is load-bearing.  feat / new / adj / blow are UPPERCASE badges;
   this one inherits .pv-mk-i's untransformed case so it reads as a note rather
   than a label — which is exactly what it is.  Do not add text-transform here.

   Contrast is the row's established floor, not a new claim: .pv-mk-i already ships
   raw var(--muted) ink for `lane` chips, over a 10% muted wash.  Dropping the wash
   moves the backdrop AWAY from the ink in BOTH themes (the wash lightens a dark
   panel and darkens a light one), so this chip reads at or above the shipped lane
   chip everywhere.  Never "tidy" it by giving it a tint — the missing fill is the
   whole idea. #}
.pv-mk-nck{background:transparent;color:var(--muted);
  border-style:dashed;border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 42%,transparent)}
{# a marks chip carrying a data-tip is a hover target, not a link — say so #}
.pv-mk-i[data-tip-en]{cursor:help}
.pv-stp{display:flex;align-items:center;margin:7px 1px 0}
.pv-dot{width:6.5px;height:6.5px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--line);flex:none}
.pv-seg{flex:1;height:2px;background:var(--line);opacity:.75}
.pv-dot.pa,.pv-seg.pa{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 45%,var(--line));opacity:1}
.pv-dot.on{background:var(--pvh);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 18%,transparent)}
.pv-stl{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:3px;margin-top:3px;min-width:0}
.pv-stl span{font-size:9.5px;color:var(--muted);opacity:.7;white-space:nowrap}
.pv-stl span.on{color:var(--pvh);opacity:1;font-weight:700}
{#- ── THE ZONE SHELF FOLDS, IT DOES NOT TRUNCATE (2026-09-02, Chairman report) ──
   `flex-wrap:wrap` is the whole redesign. The shelf is a two-end table row —
   [ZONE][value] …………… [Added Aug 31] — and its right end is provenance, not
   price. Before this, the row was a single unwrappable line in which the
   metadata was the only shrinkable child, so on a dense grid the chip did not
   yield space, it DISSOLVED: measured on the live board at the 2-up narrow
   grid (154px cards) the EN chip rendered at 5px ("Added A…" → nothing) and
   the ZH chip at 18–29px ("入.."), and at the desktop `minmax(246px,1fr)`
   floor the widest real US zone string ($1111.10–$1147.20) left 224px of room
   for 224.4px of content — a coin flip decided by the reader's font metrics,
   which is exactly the "Adde…" the Chairman saw.
   Truncating a 12-character date is worse than not printing it: "Added A…"
   states a fact the reader cannot use and reads as a rendering fault, and this
   card already has an honest, shipped vocabulary for "we can't say" — the null
   renders NOTHING. So the chip is no longer allowed to shrink at all. When the
   line cannot hold both, the chip drops to its own line, still hard against the
   right edge, and renders in full. The price keeps first claim on line one and
   is untouched (F1 stands, and `.pv-znm` is hardened to match `.pv-znr` below,
   closing the one value path F1 never covered).
   row-gap is 2px so the fold reads as the same shelf hugging under its number
   rather than a new row; the 5px column-gap is unchanged. -#}
.pv-zn{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:2px 5px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--panel) 55%,var(--bg));border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 10px 7px;font-size:10.5px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;margin-top:auto}
.pv-znl{font-size:9.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh));flex:none}
{#- R4 (2026-09-01 repair round 3): flex:none stands (the F1 fix — the CHIP
   degrades first, never the price) but a BARE flex:none has no size ceiling
   of its own, so a pathologically long zone string (e.g. a wide "lo–hi"
   range) could overflow `.pv-zn`'s row and get hard-clipped mid-character by
   its `overflow:hidden`, with no ellipsis — an UNSIGNALLED clip. max-width:
   100%;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis gives .pv-znr its own bounded
   overflow so that far-edge case degrades with a visible "…" instead,
   without reintroducing flex-shrink (which is what let the chips crowd the
   price out pre-F1). #}
.pv-znr{font-weight:700;flex:none;max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
{#- 2026-09-02: `.pv-znm` — the muted value variant — now carries the SAME
   contract as `.pv-znr`. F1 named this the one value path its repair never
   hardened, and the fold above is what makes closing it necessary rather than
   merely tidy: with the chip no longer shrinkable, a `min-width:0` value slot
   would have become the sole absorber of the squeeze, so a card with a muted
   range or a stance sentence ("No zone — stand aside") plus a chip would have
   started clipping the STANCE to protect the metadata — precisely inverted.
   flex:none + its own bounded max-width:100% ellipsis makes both value
   variants unshrinkable-but-self-bounded, so metadata always yields first. -#}
.pv-znm{color:var(--muted);flex:none;max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
{#- `.pv-dt` (legacy per-row PLAN-card date) is deliberately UNCHANGED: it keeps
   min-width:0 + ellipsis, so it still shrinks to nothing before the shelf folds
   and plan cards keep their prior geometry exactly. Only `.pv-added` — the
   board-membership chip this packet owns — opts into the fold. -#}
.pv-dt{margin-left:auto;color:var(--muted);flex:0 1 auto;min-width:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;font-size:9.5px;padding-left:5px}
{#- flex:0 0 auto (never shrink) + NO overflow/ellipsis: the two halves of one
   decision. Keeping `overflow:hidden` here would have quietly defeated the
   first half — a flex item whose overflow is not `visible` resolves
   `min-width:auto` to 0, so it would still have collapsed to 5px instead of
   wrapping. The chip is now either fully legible or on its own line; it has no
   truncated state left to render.
   `padding-left` is dropped with it. `margin-left:auto` already pins the chip
   to the far right, and the shelf's own 5px column-gap is the same separation
   `.pv-znl`↔`.pv-znr` use — the extra 5px was belt-and-braces that cost exactly
   the room the fold was being triggered by. Removing it buys back ~4.6px of
   headroom at the 246px desktop floor, so the widest real US zone string now
   fits on ONE line there with margin instead of folding on a font-metric coin
   flip. On the 2-up narrow grid it still folds — correctly, that row has no
   room for both at any padding. -#}
.pv-added{margin-left:auto;color:var(--muted);flex:0 0 auto;font-size:9.5px;line-height:1.3}
.pv-dt+.pv-added{margin-left:5px}
.pv-trg{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:2px;font-size:10px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.35;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh) 9%,var(--panel));color:var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh));border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--pvh-ink,var(--pvh)) 45%,transparent)}
.pv-trg.pv-trg-soon{border-style:dashed;opacity:.92}
.pv-cau{position:relative;display:inline-flex}
.pv-cau-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:3px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.35;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:999px;cursor:pointer;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn) 14%,var(--panel));color:var(--ink-warn,var(--warn));border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink-warn,var(--warn)) 40%,transparent);font-family:inherit}
{# Wider than the old 190-250px: these rows are full sentences now, and at 190px a
   two-clause caution wrapped to four lines. Height is capped and scrolls rather than
   growing without limit — a name can carry six or more cautions. #}
.pv-cau-pop{display:none;position:absolute;top:calc(100% + 6px);left:0;z-index:30;width:264px;max-width:min(264px,78vw);max-height:min(300px,58vh);overflow-y:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:9px 11px 10px;box-shadow:var(--popover-shadow);white-space:normal;text-align:left}
.pv-cau:hover .pv-cau-pop,.pv-cau:focus-within .pv-cau-pop{display:block}
.pv-cau-hd{display:block;margin:0 0 7px;font-size:8.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-warn, var(--warn))}
{# Bulleted, not hairline-ruled: five ledger rows read as a table of equals; a bullet
   list reads as notes and lets each row keep its own sentence rhythm. #}
.pv-cau-row{position:relative;display:block;padding-left:12px;font-size:10.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--text)}
.pv-cau-row::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:2px;top:6.5px;width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--warn);opacity:.7}
.pv-cau-row + .pv-cau-row{margin-top:7px}
{# PROPHET LIVE P1 (spec §5.3) — the ◐ live chip. Reserved empty slot in every overlay,
   filled client-side from live/prophet_live.json (dashboard.html.j2, mode=stocks only).
   NOT --pvh: this chip is today's tape, not the nightly verdict (see the macro header). #}
.pv-live{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:3px;font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1.35;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap;--plvc:#62a0e8;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--plvc) 12%,var(--panel));color:var(--plvc);border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--plvc) 44%,transparent)}
{# MANDATORY. A class-level `display` out-specifies the UA [hidden] rule, so without this
   line every card on every prophet board grows an empty mystery pill. Verified by
   computed style (tests/test_prophet_live_surface.py pins the rule's presence). #}
.pv-live[hidden]{display:none}
html[data-theme="light"] .pv-live{--plvc:#2f6fd0}
{# NOT solid-filled, unlike the strip's .plv-chip--close: a solid pill out-weighs an
   outlined verb chip, and the card's verb must stay its ruling stance (macro law). The
   fill escalation lives on the strip, where a cross is news and has no verb to outrank. #}
.pv-live--close{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--plvc) 18%,var(--panel));border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--plvc) 70%,transparent)}
.pv-live--drop,.pv-live--over{--plvc:var(--pv-wait)}
{#- P-MP1-SHELL: .pv-life / .pv-newer / .pv-mark CSS deliberately does NOT live
   here. This macro (pv_css()) is called by EVERY board — hk/china/canada/intl
   included (each does `{% import "_prophet_card.html.j2" as pv %}` +
   `{{ pv.pv_css() }}`) — and MP-1 §7/§12 item 3 require those pages' rendered
   bytes to stay byte-identical. Adding CSS here would change their <style>
   block even though the markup that CSS supports (pv_card's `lifecycle`/
   `lane_mark` params) is exercised only by the US template. That CSS lives in
   templates/dashboard.html.j2's own <style> block instead — the same
   non-shared placement §9's restated "theme.css" law and this packet's other
   template-scoped primitives already use. See dashboard.html.j2 for
   .pv-life/.pv-life-w/.pv-newer/.pv-mark. #}
[data-showmore-rows] .pvcard .pv-chart svg,[data-showmore-rows] .pvcard .pv-nochart{height:56px}
[data-showmore-rows] .pvcard .pv-tk{font-size:11.5px}
[data-showmore-rows] .pvcard .pv-stl span{font-size:9px}
[data-showmore-rows] .pvcard .pv-mk{margin-top:3px}
@media (min-width:681px){
  .nbgrid:has(> .pvcard),.cards:has(> .pvcard),.rip-grid:has(> .pvcard){grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(246px,1fr))!important}
}
@media (max-width:680px){
  .pvcard .pv-chart svg,.pvcard .pv-nochart{height:58px}
{# System display zoom reduces the effective CSS width. Keep the ticker + Edge
   score on the first line and give the company name its own full-width line;
   otherwise flex shrink can collapse .pv-nm to zero on narrow two-up cards. #}
  .pv-hd{align-items:flex-start}
  .pv-idw{flex:1 1 auto;flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:1px;overflow:visible}
  .pv-nm{flex-basis:100%;width:100%}
  .pv-stl span{font-size:9px}
  .pv-zn{font-size:10px}
  {#- The ≤680px `.pv-added{max-width:32%}` cap is GONE (2026-09-02). It was the
     mechanism that made the chip start truncating EARLY so the price reliably
     won the line — a correct priority implemented with the wrong verb. At the
     2-up narrow grid (154px cards) 32% of the row is ~42px against a 66px
     chip, i.e. the cap guaranteed a truncated date on every phone card that
     carried one. The fold (see .pv-zn / .pv-added above) enforces the same
     priority — price first, metadata yields — without ever rendering a partial
     date, so the cap has nothing left to do and would now only re-impose the
     defect on the folded line, where the chip has the whole row.
     `.pv-znr` keeps flex:none and its own bounded overflow; F1 is unchanged and
     `.pv-znm` is now hardened to match it. `.pv-dt` is untouched here, exactly
     as R5 left it. #}
  /* narrow cards: trigger chip collapses to the bare ⚡ glyph (the board copy
     teaches "marked ⚡"); !important outranks the html[data-lang] l-en/l-zh
     visibility rules, which otherwise win at any width. The overlay's own
     flex-wrap now applies at EVERY width (promoted above — it was a desktop
     clipping bug), so it is no longer repeated here. */
  .pv-trg .l-en,.pv-trg .l-zh{display:none!important}
  .pv-trg{padding:2px 5px;gap:0}
  /* same collapse-to-glyph rule for the ◐ live chip */
  .pv-live .l-en,.pv-live .l-zh{display:none!important}
  .pv-live{padding:2px 5px;gap:0}
  /* marks chips do NOT collapse to a glyph — "Featured" and the theme name are
     the words that make the row non-colour-only; they get one size UP instead,
     because a phone is where 9.5px stops being readable. */
  .pv-mk-i{font-size:10px;padding:2px 7px}
}
</style>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro pv_card(cx, allow_no_read=false) %}
{%- set _VEN = {'buy':'Buy','near':'Near','wait':'Wait','hold':'Hold','avoid':'Avoid'} -%}
{%- set _VZH = {'buy':'买入','near':'临近','wait':'等待','hold':'持有','avoid':'回避'} -%}
{%- set _MN = {'01':'Jan','02':'Feb','03':'Mar','04':'Apr','05':'May','06':'Jun','07':'Jul','08':'Aug','09':'Sep','10':'Oct','11':'Nov','12':'Dec'} -%}
{#- P-MP1-SHELL §8a (b1 ruling, macro wait-default parameterization requirement):
    the ORIGINAL fallback below silently rendered "wait" for any unrecognized/absent
    verb — exactly the default DESIGN_NOTES.md Q7b forbids for an unobtainable
    stance (BLOCKED_DATA must render as a disclosed no-read chip, never a guessed
    Wait). `allow_no_read` is additive and OFF by default: every existing caller
    (hk/china/canada/intl, and every current US call site) passes no such flag and
    keeps this exact byte-for-byte fallback-to-wait behavior. Only a caller that
    explicitly opts in AND passes a verb that fails the `_VEN` membership test
    (i.e. `cx.verb` is None/absent — the no_read basis from us_stance_projection())
    takes the new branch. -#}
{%- set _no_read = allow_no_read and (cx.verb not in _VEN) -%}
{%- set _verb = 'wait' if _no_read else (cx.verb if cx.verb in _VEN else 'wait') -%}
{%- set _stage = cx.get('stage') or 0 -%}
<a class="pvcard{% if _no_read %} pv-noread{% else %} pv-{{ _verb }}{% endif %}{% if cx.get('featured') %} pv-featured{% elif cx.get('triage') %} pv-triage{% endif %}" href="{{ cx.href|e }}"{% if cx.get('id') %} id="pv-{{ cx.id|e }}"{% endif %} data-ticker="{{ cx.tk|e }}"{% if cx.get('life') %} data-life="{{ cx.life|e }}"{% endif %}{% if cx.get('stage_key') %} data-stage="{{ cx.stage_key|e }}"{% endif %}{% if cx.get('stance_basis') %} data-tip-en="{{ cx.get('stance_tip_en') or ('Stance source: ' ~ cx.stance_basis) }}" data-tip-zh="{{ cx.get('stance_tip_zh') or ('依据来源：' ~ cx.stance_basis) }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="pv-chart">
    {% if cx.get('spark') %}{{ cx.spark|safe }}{% else %}<div class="pv-nochart"></div>{% endif %}
    <span class="pv-ov pv-ovl">
      {#- NO popover on the verb chip (operator 2026-08-05, extending the 2026-08-03
          removal). BUY/WAIT/NEAR is a one-word ruling and the card already spells out
          the same thing underneath — the stage rail, the zone row and the ⚠ notes — so
          "Constructive — building a base · Buy zone — entry open now" bought nothing and
          put a popover over the neighbouring card on the way. `cx.tip_en`/`tip_zh` are
          still accepted by callers; they are simply not rendered. Same call for .pv-edge
          and the feat/new marks below. The ⚡ trigger tip and the ⚠N popover STAY: those
          carry facts that appear nowhere else on the card. -#}
      <span class="pv-chip"{% if _no_read %} data-noread="1"{% endif %}>{% if _no_read %}{{ t('No read yet', '暂无读数') }}{% else %}{{ t(_VEN[_verb], _VZH[_verb]) }}{% endif %}</span>
      {%- if cx.get('trigger') %}{% set _tg = cx.trigger %}
      <span class="pv-trg{% if _tg.kind == 'imminent' %} pv-trg-soon{% endif %}"{% if _tg.get('tip_en') %} data-tip-en="{{ _tg.tip_en|e }}" data-tip-zh="{{ (_tg.get('tip_zh') or _tg.tip_en)|e }}"{% endif %}>⚡ {% if _tg.kind == 'imminent' %}{{ t('Imminent','即将触发') }}{% else %}{{ t('Triggered','已触发') }}{% endif %}</span>
      {%- endif %}
      {#- PROPHET LIVE P1 (spec §5.2): reserved, always-present, EMPTY slot for the ◐ live
          chip. The card is server-rendered nightly and the live state arrives every ~5
          minutes, so this chip cannot be SSR'd — dashboard.html.j2's strip JS fills it by
          .pvcard[data-ticker]. `hidden` + the .pv-live[hidden] rule in pv_css() means zero
          width and zero layout change when there is no live state, which is every card on
          every non-us_stocks board and most cards here. #}
      <span class="pv-live" hidden></span>
      {%- if cx.get('flags') %}
      <span class="pv-cau"><button class="pv-cau-btn" type="button" aria-label="Caution notes ({{ cx.flags|length }})" onclick="event.preventDefault();event.stopPropagation();this.focus()">⚠ {{ cx.flags|length }}</button><span class="pv-cau-pop" role="tooltip"><span class="pv-cau-hd">{{ t('Before you act','动手之前') }}</span>{% for _f in cx.flags %}<span class="pv-cau-row">{{ t(_f[0], _f[1]) }}</span>{% endfor %}</span></span>
      {%- endif %}
    </span>
    {% if cx.get('price_txt') %}<span class="pv-ov pv-ovr">{% if cx.get('show_change') %}<span class="pv-quote"><span class="nb-px pv-px" data-sym="{{ (cx.get('sym') or cx.tk)|e }}" data-mkt="{{ cx.mkt|e }}">{{ cx.price_txt }}</span><span class="nb-chg pv-chg" data-sym="{{ (cx.get('sym') or cx.tk)|e }}" data-mkt="{{ cx.mkt|e }}">—</span></span>{% else %}<span class="nb-px pv-px" data-sym="{{ (cx.get('sym') or cx.tk)|e }}" data-mkt="{{ cx.mkt|e }}">{{ cx.price_txt }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="pv-bd">
    <div class="pv-hd">
      <span class="pv-idw">{% if cx.get('flag') %}<span class="pv-flg">{{ cx.flag }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="pv-tk">{{ cx.tk }}</span>{% if cx.get('name') %}<span class="pv-nm">{{ t(cx.name, cx.get('name_zh') or cx.name) }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="pv-edge"><span class="pv-edl">{{ t(cx.get('edge_label_en') or 'Edge', cx.get('edge_label_zh') or '优势') }}</span>{% if cx.get('edge') is not none %}<span class="pv-edn">{{ cx.edge }}</span>{% elif cx.get('edge_txt') %}<span class="pv-edn">{{ cx.edge_txt }}</span>{% else %}<span class="pv-edn pv-edna">—</span>{% endif %}</span>
    </div>
    {% if cx.get('sec') %}<div class="pv-ind">{{ t(cx.sec, cx.get('sec_zh') or cx.sec) }}</div>{% endif %}
    {%- if cx.get('lane_mark') %}{% set _lm = cx.lane_mark %}<span class="pv-mark" tabindex="0" data-tip-en="{{ _lm.tip_en|e }}" data-tip-zh="{{ (_lm.get('tip_zh') or _lm.tip_en)|e }}">{{ t(_lm.en, _lm.get('zh') or _lm.en) }}</span>{% endif %}
    {%- if cx.get('marks') is not none %}
    {#- FEATURED and NEW carry no popover (operator 2026-08-05): both are badges whose
        whole job is to be read at a glance, and their explainers were the longest cards
        on the board. Marks that genuinely name something the reader cannot infer (warm,
        theme, lane) keep theirs. -#}
    {%- set _MK_NOTIP = ('feat', 'new') -%}
    <div class="pv-mk">{% for _mk in cx.marks %}{% set _mkk = _mk.get('k') or 'lane' %}<span class="pv-mk-i pv-mk-{{ _mkk }}"{% if _mk.get('tip_en') and _mkk not in _MK_NOTIP %} data-tip-en="{{ _mk.tip_en|e }}" data-tip-zh="{{ (_mk.get('tip_zh') or _mk.tip_en)|e }}"{% endif %}>{{ t(_mk.en, _mk.get('zh') or _mk.en) }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>
    {%- endif %}
    {#- P-MP1-SHELL §6 (ruling §10.1): on the lifecycle-sourced call path
        (cx.lifecycle present), the 4-dot Bottoming/Turning/Ready/Trend rail is
        REPLACED by the lifecycle fact row (.mx-mark + word + optional
        newer-plan link) — same-PR removal, per-card, additive: every caller
        that omits `lifecycle` keeps the 4-dot rail byte-identical
        (§12 acceptance item 3). -#}
    {%- if cx.get('lifecycle') %}{% set _lc = cx.lifecycle %}
    <div class="pv-life"><span class="mx-mark mx-mark--{{ _lc.state|e }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="pv-life-w">{{ t(_lc.label_en, _lc.label_zh) }}</span>{% if _lc.get('newer') %}<a class="pv-newer" href="#pv-{{ _lc.newer|e }}">{{ t('Newer plan on this name →', '该股最新计划 →') }}</a>{% endif %}</div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="pv-stp">{% for _i in [1,2,3,4] %}{% if _i > 1 %}<span class="pv-seg{% if _stage >= _i %} pa{% endif %}"></span>{% endif %}<span class="pv-dot{% if _stage == _i %} on{% elif _stage > _i %} pa{% endif %}"></span>{% endfor %}</div>
    <div class="pv-stl"><span{% if _stage == 1 %} class="on"{% endif %}>{{ t('Bottoming','筑底') }}</span><span{% if _stage == 2 %} class="on"{% endif %}>{{ t('Turning','转向') }}</span><span{% if _stage == 3 %} class="on"{% endif %}>{{ t('Ready','就绪') }}</span><span{% if _stage == 4 %} class="on"{% endif %}>{{ t('Trend','趋势') }}</span></div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="pv-zn">
    {%- set _zk = cx.get('zone_kind') or 'none' -%}
    {%- if _zk == 'active' -%}
    <span class="pv-znl">{{ t('Zone','买区') }}</span><span class="pv-znr">{{ cx.zone_lo }}{% if cx.get('zone_hi') and cx.zone_hi != cx.zone_lo %}–{{ cx.zone_hi }}{% endif %}</span>
    {%- elif _zk == 'muted' -%}
    <span class="pv-znl">{{ t('Zone','买区') }}</span><span class="pv-znm">{{ cx.zone_lo }}{% if cx.get('zone_hi') and cx.zone_hi != cx.zone_lo %}–{{ cx.zone_hi }}{% endif %}</span>
    {%- elif _zk == 'readd' -%}
    <span class="pv-znl">{{ t('Re-add','回补') }}</span><span class="pv-znm">{{ cx.zone_lo }}{% if cx.get('zone_hi') and cx.zone_hi != cx.zone_lo %}–{{ cx.zone_hi }}{% endif %}</span>
    {%- elif _zk == 'confirm' -%}
    <span class="pv-znm">{{ t('Zone sets on confirmation','买区待确认后生成') }}</span>
    {%- elif _zk == 'note' -%}
    <span class="pv-znm">{{ t(cx.get('zone_note_en') or '—', cx.get('zone_note_zh') or cx.get('zone_note_en') or '—') }}</span>
    {%- else -%}
    <span class="pv-znm">{{ t('No zone — stand aside','无买区 — 观望') }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- set _d = cx.get('date') -%}
    {%- if _d and _d|length >= 10 %}<span class="pv-dt">{{ t(_MN.get(_d[5:7], _d[5:7]) ~ ' ' ~ (_d[8:10]|int), _d[5:10]) }}</span>{% endif %}
    {#- Added / 入榜 — current continuous published-board membership start
        (engine/prophet_board_since.py). STRICT ISO gate: anything shorter or
        longer than exactly 10 chars, or not matching the YYYY-MM-DD shape at
        positions 4/7, renders NOTHING — no "Added —" placeholder, no fallback.
        Unlike `date` this is never derived from an as-of/build-date/wall-clock
        constant; a market whose history cannot prove a start date ships null,
        and null is silent here by design (frozen spec: "unknown/unprovable ⇒
        None and NO chip"). -#}
    {%- set _ad = cx.get('added_date') -%}
    {%- if _ad and _ad|length == 10 and _ad[4] == '-' and _ad[7] == '-' %}<span class="pv-added" data-added="{{ _ad|e }}" data-tip-en="On the Prophet board continuously since this date. If the name leaves and later returns, this date resets." data-tip-zh="自该日起持续在 Prophet 榜上；若离榜后重新上榜，此日期将重新计算。">{{ t('Added ' ~ _MN.get(_ad[5:7], _ad[5:7]) ~ ' ' ~ (_ad[8:10]|int), '入榜 ' ~ _ad[5:10]) }}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
</a>
{% endmacro %}
